    [BugFix][CI] Run GLM5_1_W4A4_A5 on V2 with intra-RoCE off (#19081)
    
    The A5 nightly case `GLM5_1_W4A4_A5` failed in
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/38845919751/job/116797872532
    while running Model Runner V2 with intra-node RoCE enabled. This PR
    reruns that case on V2 with intra-RoCE turned off.
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    `tests/e2e/cases/models/configs/GLM/GLM5_1_W4A4_A5.yaml` changes two
    environment variables:
    
    - `VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER`: `"0"` to `"1"`. Current main pins V1 while
    keeping `prefill-context-parallel-size` 4, so V1 rejects the case before
    startup. V2 accepts PCP, which is the shape that job ran.
    - `HCCL_INTRA_ROCE_ENABLE`: `"1"` to `"0"`.
    
    TP, PCP, and the EPLB server flags are unchanged.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This only changes the nightly environment for this case.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - YAML parse of
    `tests/e2e/cases/models/configs/GLM/GLM5_1_W4A4_A5.yaml`. The loaded env
    is `VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=1` and `HCCL_INTRA_ROCE_ENABLE=0`.
    - Not run on NPU. After review, rerun with `/nightly GLM5_1_W4A4_A5`.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
    Signed-off-by: yjyang62 <yjyang62@users.noreply.github.com>
    Co-authored-by: yjyang62 <yjyang62@users.noreply.github.com>

